This is a '''list of [[Regions of Balisca|Baliscan regions]] by [[W:Gross domestic product|gross domestic product]]'''. Regional statistics are estimates of economic activity at the regional level calculated in accordance with Balisca's confederal accounts.

== Methodology ==
The article lists the [[Gross domestic product|GDP]] of Baliscan regions in main [[W:Fiscal year|fiscal years]], where all figures are obtained from the [[Instituto Confederal de Stadística]] (ICS). Calculating GDP of Baliscan regions is based on [[Baliscan sol]] (S/), for easy comparison, all the GDP figures are converted into [[United States dollar]] (US$) according to current annual average exchange rates.

Note that due to constant changes in sol/dollar rates, GDP may not reflect relative economic strength in foreign currency terms, meaning that comparisons between years and regions are most meaningful in the local currency, the sol.

In 2025, the sol/dollar rate is 1.3333 (average), valuing Balisca's nominal 2025 GDP figure of '''9.01 trillion sol''', at '''US $6.76 trillion'''.
